---
title: Guinness Barbecue Sauce
description: This one's all original.
source.name: 100% Original
tags: Alcohol, Originals, Sides
---

> This recipe scales up nicely for canning and preserving. It is a great sauce to have on hand for grilling season.

Bring @Guinness Stout{22%oz} and @brown sugar{3/4%cup} to a light boil over medium-high heat, stirring occasionally.

Add the @tomato paste{15%oz}, @Worcestershire Sauce{3%Tbsp}, @honey{2%Tbsp}, and @cider vinegar{1.25%cup} to the pot.

Combine the @dried minced onion{2%Tbsp}, @garlic powder{2%Tbsp}, @rubbed sage{1.5%Tbsp},
@salt{2%tsp}, @Penzey's Hot Curry Powder{1%Tbsp}, @cayenne pepper{1%Tbsp}(ground),
@allspice{1%Tbsp}(ground), @cumin{1.5%Tbsp}(ground), and @ground ginger{2%tsp}
in a small bowl and mix well.

Add the spice mixture and return to a boil.

Reduce heat and simmer uncovered for ~{30%minutes}, stirring regularly, or until reduced to desired thickness.

Cool before using.
Brush on ribs or chicken.
